# Deployment safeguard (mandatory)

Independent source work may happen concurrently. Independent deployment to a
shared staging or production target may not overwrite another workstream.

Use official safe deployment tooling only:

- `node scripts/deployment-guard/preflight.mjs`
- `node scripts/deployment-guard/lease.mjs`
- `node scripts/deployment-guard/lambda-overlay.mjs`
- `node scripts/deployment-guard/spa-promote.mjs`
- `node scripts/deployment-guard/sql-apply.mjs`
- `node scripts/deployment-guard/verify-live.mjs`
- `node scripts/deployment-guard/manifest.mjs`
- `node scripts/production-deploy-guard.mjs` (production fingerprint vs release-locks)

Never deploy directly when this guarded tooling exists.

Shared-target writers refuse with `DEPLOYMENT_GUARD_REQUIRED` unless a
short-lived receipt exists for this workstream, environment, component,
commit, live fingerprint, lease, and owned files. A staging Lambda receipt
does not authorize SPA or production. An environment variable cannot bypass
this.

Never:

- reclaim an environment
- reuse an old Lambda ZIP, `/tmp` package, stale `dist`, or previous SPA build
- overwrite another workstream's live members
- put an old `index.html` back
- restore a previous baseline because "we were here first"
- `aws lambda update-function-code` against `checksops-staging-api` or `checksops-production-prep-api` outside the overlay evaluator
- `sam deploy` a thin template over a live overlay Lambda
- infer production approval from a previous workstream

If live state changed after preflight (CodeSha256, RevisionId, index.html, SQL
definition): **STOP** with `DEPLOYMENT_COLLISION`. Do not reclaim.

If two workstreams changed the same Lambda member: **STOP** with
`SOURCE_RECONCILIATION_REQUIRED` and reconcile in source.

If multiple workstreams contain frontend changes: **STOP** with
`SOURCE_COMPOSITION_REQUIRED` and build one combined candidate.

Preserve unrelated work. Overlay only declared owned members onto a freshly
downloaded live package.

This rule supplements enforcement in `scripts/deployment-guard/`. It is not
the only safeguard. Do not deploy this guard. Do not change AWS, staging,
production, or database data unless a separately reviewed apply workstream
explicitly authorizes it.
